    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "I got targeted: Trying to get your credentials via a git post-checkout hook",
      "url": "https://frankwiles.com/posts/i-got-targeted/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/cd5gdk",
      "score": 95,
      "comments": 32,
      "author": "frankwiles",
      "published": "2026-10-02T22:19:02Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Threat actors weaponize git post-checkout hooks, abusing submodules or setup scripts, to execute arbitrary code automatically upon branch switching.",
        "Injected scripts systematically exfiltrate developer secrets, specifically targeting ~/.aws credentials, SSH private keys, environment variables, and git credential helpers.",
        "Mitigate hook-based execution globally by configuring `core.hooksPath` to /dev/null and isolating untrusted repository inspection inside sandboxed containers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "devops",
      "title": "Cloudflare OHTTP gateway",
      "url": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/announcing-cloudflare-ohttp-gateway/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49941091",
      "score": 176,
      "comments": 81,
      "author": "est",
      "published": "2026-10-03T03:15:05Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Cloudflare implements RFC 9458 Oblivious HTTP, separating client IP metadata from application payloads using HPKE-encrypted requests routed through intermediary relays.",
        "Enables teams to ingest client telemetry, analytics, and metrics at scale without logging or processing sensitive end-user IP addresses.",
        "The gateway terminates HPKE encryption before proxying plain HTTP to origins, reducing compliance burden for privacy-focused edge infrastructure."
      ]
    },
